    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d328">

                <pb facs="0452" n="1206" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg1206"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 611.529/171</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-09-10T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 10, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5408. Your 7127, September 7.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d328-f1"/> Inform Foreign
                    Office that Department has already made investigation of domestic sulphur
                    supplies which indicates that latter are being utilized to full extent and are
                    not capable of increased production at present. United States in urgent need of
                    quantities of Spanish pyrites in addition thereto and no present prospect of
                    reduction of requirements therefor.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
